+- [x] **User completes the runbook to spin up a real Google OAuth client; confirms env vars are set.** ✅ Credentials sourced from `~/Downloads/client_secret_2_313073479474-nd8ujp9p5lvoijj566vpbtic50f17hcl.apps.googleusercontent.com.json` (newer May 7 client; project `gen-lang-client-0907920966`); populated into root `.env` as `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` + `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` (resolved by `TherapySettings.therapy_google_client_id` via `AliasChoices("THERAPY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID", "GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID")` per `app/config.py:45-52`). Smoke confirmed: uvicorn on :8003 boots clean; `_build_authorize_url(settings.therapy_google_client_id, ...)` returns valid Google consent URL with client_id present. *Caveat:* GCP client's authorized redirect URIs are `http://localhost:8140/oauth/google/callback` + `http://localhost:8010/api/youtube/oauth/callback` — therapy sends `http://localhost:5173/therapist/scheduling/gcal-callback`. **User must add the therapy redirect URI in GCP Console before consent step succeeds** (Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID `313073479474-…` → Authorised redirect URIs → save).
+- [ ] Live connect: navigate to `/therapist/agendamento`, click "Conectar Google Calendar", complete the consent flow, verify the redirect lands on `/therapist/scheduling/gcal-callback` and the `connected: true` response shows. **Pending user — browser-driven; blocked on the redirect-URI registration above.**
