+**Improvements:**
+- The runbook (`KB § GUIDES/google-oauth-setup.md`) documents `THERAPY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `THERAPY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` as the env-var names, but the platform-wide convention added 2026-05-11 (`app/config.py:39-42` comment block) is to use root-`.env` `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` / `_SECRET` with per-product prefix as an override. Both work via the AliasChoices wiring; the runbook is slightly stale — its Step 5 should note the platform-wide default. Captured here as a Phase 4 polish item (one-line edit; defer to a future docs pass since no current consumer is hitting the gap).
+- The two `client_secret_*.json` files in `~/Downloads/` represent two distinct GCP OAuth clients (May 2 + May 7) sharing the same client_id but different secrets and redirect_uris. The May 7 (`_2`) variant was chosen because it matches the existing `GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8140/oauth/google/callback` line already in root `.env`. The May 2 variant only registered `http://localhost:8000/oauth/google/callback`. If multiple products end up sharing one client, the redirect_uri list grows monotonically — the runbook should flag this; tracked here.
 
